{
  "format": "asakiri-course",
  "formatVersion": 2,
  "type": "doc",
  "content": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            },
            {
              "type": "underline"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Quick Grammar Notes / Particles"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "や or ぬ? [Warning: Bulk Text]"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "There are many ways to explain this and people could easily search up the differences between は and が in Japanese, since that’s their equivalent, but here is how this course will explain it. ぬ can also be used for possession. Vocabulary used as examples for this section should be words at this level and you should have learned."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "や is used under one of two conditions:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "orderedList",
      "attrs": {
        "start": 1,
        "type": null
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "listItem",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "It’s the topic of the sentence."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "orderedList",
              "attrs": {
                "start": 1,
                "type": null
              },
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "listItem",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "paragraph",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "NOTE! Often times, you can put something like “Regarding” or “About” in front of the noun to make it make sense."
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "orderedList",
                      "attrs": {
                        "start": 1,
                        "type": null
                      },
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "listItem",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Ex. 砂糖（さーたー）や　甘（あま）さん。"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "listItem",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Translation: Sugar is sweet."
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "listItem",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "For the NOTE! you can see this sentence like: "
                                },
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "marks": [
                                    {
                                      "type": "bold"
                                    }
                                  ],
                                  "text": "Regarding"
                                },
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": " sugar, it is sweet."
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "listItem",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Often times, it becomes longer, there’s a 〜や〜ぬ sentence structure often times. Basically a simple sentence with two particles are often times や followed by ぬ"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "listItem",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Ex. 　"
                                },
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "marks": [
                                    {
                                      "type": "underline"
                                    }
                                  ],
                                  "text": "いぃー"
                                },
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "marks": [
                                    {
                                      "type": "bold"
                                    }
                                  ],
                                  "text": "日（ふぃー）"
                                },
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "や　"
                                },
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "marks": [
                                    {
                                      "type": "bold"
                                    }
                                  ],
                                  "text": "あま"
                                },
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "marks": [
                                    {
                                      "type": "textStyle",
                                      "attrs": {
                                        "color": "rgb(0, 0, 0)"
                                      }
                                    },
                                    {
                                      "type": "bold"
                                    }
                                  ],
                                  "text": "ぬ"
                                },
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "marks": [
                                    {
                                      "type": "textStyle",
                                      "attrs": {
                                        "color": "rgb(0, 0, 0)"
                                      }
                                    }
                                  ],
                                  "text": "　すばぬ　まーさん。"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "listItem",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "marks": [
                                    {
                                      "type": "textStyle",
                                      "attrs": {
                                        "color": "rgb(0, 0, 0)"
                                      }
                                    }
                                  ],
                                  "text": "Translation: On a "
                                },
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "marks": [
                                    {
                                      "type": "textStyle",
                                      "attrs": {
                                        "color": "rgb(0, 0, 0)"
                                      }
                                    },
                                    {
                                      "type": "underline"
                                    }
                                  ],
                                  "text": "good"
                                },
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "marks": [
                                    {
                                      "type": "textStyle",
                                      "attrs": {
                                        "color": "rgb(0, 0, 0)"
                                      }
                                    }
                                  ],
                                  "text": " "
                                },
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "marks": [
                                    {
                                      "type": "textStyle",
                                      "attrs": {
                                        "color": "rgb(0, 0, 0)"
                                      }
                                    },
                                    {
                                      "type": "bold"
                                    }
                                  ],
                                  "text": "day"
                                },
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "marks": [
                                    {
                                      "type": "textStyle",
                                      "attrs": {
                                        "color": "rgb(0, 0, 0)"
                                      }
                                    }
                                  ],
                                  "text": ", the (Okinawa) soba "
                                },
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "marks": [
                                    {
                                      "type": "textStyle",
                                      "attrs": {
                                        "color": "rgb(0, 0, 0)"
                                      }
                                    },
                                    {
                                      "type": "bold"
                                    }
                                  ],
                                  "text": "from over there"
                                },
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "marks": [
                                    {
                                      "type": "textStyle",
                                      "attrs": {
                                        "color": "rgb(0, 0, 0)"
                                      }
                                    }
                                  ],
                                  "text": " is delicious."
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "listItem",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "You can notice that the "
                                },
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "marks": [
                                    {
                                      "type": "textStyle",
                                      "attrs": {
                                        "color": ""
                                      }
                                    }
                                  ],
                                  "text": "“"
                                },
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "good day” is the topic and the first ぬ is for representing the possession “from over there” belonging to a (store) over there. The second ぬ is part of that 〜や〜ぬ sentence structure."
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "listItem",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Also side note that while ゆたさん means good as an adjective いぃー is a prefix for that."
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "orderedList",
      "attrs": {
        "start": 1,
        "type": null
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "listItem",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Contrasting things"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "orderedList",
              "attrs": {
                "start": 1,
                "type": null
              },
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "listItem",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "paragraph",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "This is more advanced, but when you have a contraster like “(や)しが” (but), it represents a contrast."
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "listItem",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "paragraph",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "Ex. あーりー"
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "marks": [
                            {
                              "type": "bold"
                            }
                          ],
                          "text": "や"
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "　やーにんじゅ　"
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "marks": [
                            {
                              "type": "underline"
                            }
                          ],
                          "text": "やしが"
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "、えーまー"
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "marks": [
                            {
                              "type": "bold"
                            }
                          ],
                          "text": "や"
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "　やーにんじゅ"
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "marks": [
                            {
                              "type": "bold"
                            }
                          ],
                          "text": "や"
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "　あらん。"
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "listItem",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "paragraph",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "Translation: Ari is family, but Emma is not."
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "listItem",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "paragraph",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "You can see we are contrasting Ari and Emma here."
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "ぬ is used under one of three conditions when it is not used to mark a possessive:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "orderedList",
      "attrs": {
        "start": 1,
        "type": null
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "listItem",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Inside an adverbial phrase (e.g., if~then むし + subject + ぬ + verb + らー・さー etc., this is advanced territory, so this will be skipped over for now)"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "listItem",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Inside a dependent clause."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "orderedList",
              "attrs": {
                "start": 1,
                "type": null
              },
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "listItem",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "paragraph",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "Ex. 先生（しんしー）ぬ　すむち　読（ゆ）むん。"
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "listItem",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "paragraph",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "Translation: The teacher reads a book OR (I am) reading the teacher’s book. (To clarify that it is the latter, you can put 我（わん）ねー in front of it.)"
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "listItem",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "paragraph",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "In the first situation notice that 先生（しんしー）ぬ　すむち \"Teacher (is/’s) book.” is a dependent clause because it doesn’t work like the example of 砂糖（さーたー）や　甘（あま）さん。(see や 1-1-1)."
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "listItem",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "paragraph",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "The second situation is simply just the possessive."
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "listItem",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "paragraph",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "For Japanese learners/speakers, you might be confused why this is the case, but when you say 先生が本を読む and 先生の本を読む, it’s about the teacher’s book that was either being read or written or both by the teacher, so it doesn’t matter too much in Okinawan."
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "listItem",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "After a question/interrogative word"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "orderedList",
              "attrs": {
                "start": 1,
                "type": null
              },
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "listItem",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "paragraph",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "Ex.誰（ たー）"
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "marks": [
                            {
                              "type": "bold"
                            }
                          ],
                          "text": "が"
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "　わーりー　やいびーが？"
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "listItem",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "paragraph",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "Translation: Who is Wally? (Which one of you is Wally?)"
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "listItem",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "paragraph",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "Note here that が is what ぬ is replaced by under specific circumstances, in this case, it’s because it’s a person (more on this in a future course). Also it is not や because "
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "listItem",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "paragraph",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "誰（ たー）can also mean “someone” as a sentence (not a question). In this case, you will still use が even though in English, it is not a question/interrogative word."
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Do note that while や and ぬ change depending on circumstance, the exams at this level won’t test you on that. It would be nice if you revisited the earlier lessons on other particles like (ん)かい."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    }
  ]
}
